WEBVTT

00:00:28.796 --> 00:00:29.716
on April 6th.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:29.980
Hey.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.160
1865, at an area known as Sailor's Creek in rural central Virginia, one of the final battles

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:42.510
between the Union and the Confederacy took place, further depleting General Lee's army

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.740
of northern Virginia, already tragic.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:53.120
worn out. Lee retreated westward and found himself pursued and finally cut off by General Grant in

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:59.860
the area of Appomattox Courthouse. On Palm Sunday, April 9th, Lee met Grant.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.400
to accept terms of surrender of his army,

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.770
bringing to an end four full years of struggle

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:10.470
and, for all practical purposes, ending the Civil War.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.580
Tonight, we will trace those last days...

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.950
through the eyes of two very special men of American history,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.300
Robert E. Lee and Ulysses S. Grant,

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.620
on Appomattox, The Final Four Days.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.390
Sheridan's cavalry is headed toward Appomattox Station.

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.110
